== Gengshen Month ==
In years where the last digit of the Western Calendar year is 3 or 8 (when the heavenly stem is {{ill|Guǐ|ja|癸}} or {{ill|Wu|ja|戊}}), the month of {{ill|July|ja|7月}} becomes the Gengshen {{ill|Month (Calendar)|ja|月 (暦)}}. Note that here the month may refer either to a month of the {{ill|Old Lunar Calendar|ja|旧暦}} or to a {{ill|Seasonal Month|ja|節月}} (from {{ill|Start of Autumn|ja|立秋}} until the day before {{ill|White Dew|ja|白露}}).

== Gengshen Day ==
On Gengshen days, a Gengshen Vigil ({{ill|Gengshen Vigil|ja|庚申待}}, also known as <!--please transliterate all the hiragana readings into romaji and provide the kanji--> {{ill|Gengshen Lecture|ja|庚申講}}) was held. {{main|{{ill|Gengshen Faith|ja|庚申信仰}}}}

A Gengshen day is also the {{ill|Festival Day|ja|縁日}} of {{ill|Taishakuten|ja|帝釈天}}.

=== Choosing a Day ===
Gengshen days occur on the sixth day (excluding intercalary days {{ill|Intercalary Day|ja|間日}}) of the {{ill|Hassen|ja|八専}} cycle.

