Because both the heavenly stem and earthly branch of Gengshen are of {{ill|Metal|ja|金属|lt=Metal|lt_ja=金|12=draft|12=draft}} nature, it was believed that the metal energy pervading the universe in a Gengshen year or day would render human hearts cold and unfeeling. The following combination, {{ill|Shinyuu|ja|辛酉|12=draft|12=draft}}, also being metal in nature—with Xin being of Yin energy—was thought to intensify this coldness. Consequently, Gengshen and Shinyuu were considered harbingers of political upheaval, and to avert such changes it was not uncommon to change eras for two consecutive years. For example, this occurred in the first years of {{ill|Man'en|ja|万延|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|1860|ja|1860th year|12=draft|12=draft}}) and {{ill|Bunkyu|ja|文久|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|1861|ja|1861st year|12=draft|12=draft}}).

