== Gengshen Month ==
In years where the last digit of the Western Calendar year is 3 or 8 (when the heavenly stem is {{ill|Guǐ|ja|癸|1=Mizunoto (癸)|qq=|12=draft}} or {{ill|Wu|ja|戊|1=Tsuchinoe (戊)|qq=|12=draft}}), the month of {{ill|July|ja|7月|qq=|12=draft}} becomes the Gengshen {{ill|Month (Calendar)|ja|月 (暦)|qq=|12=draft}}. Note that here the month may refer either to a month of the {{ill|Japanese Lunisolar Calendar|ja|旧暦|1=Japanese Lunisolar Calendar|1=Japanese Lunisolar Calendar|11=Japanese Lunisolar Calendar|qq=|12=draft}} or to a {{ill|Seasonal Month|ja|節月|qq=|12=draft}} (from {{ill|Start of Autumn|ja|立秋|qq=|12=draft}} until the day before {{ill|White Dew|ja|白露|qq=|12=draft}}).

== Gengshen Day ==
On Gengshen days, a Gengshen Vigil ({{ill|Gengshen Vigil|ja|庚申待|qq=|12=draft}}, also known as  {{ill|Gengshen Lecture|ja|庚申講|qq=|12=draft}}) was held. {{main|{{ill|Gengshen Faith|ja|庚申信仰|qq=|12=draft}}|qq=}}

A Gengshen day is also the {{ill|Festival Day|ja|縁日|qq=|12=draft}} of {{ill|Taishakuten|ja|帝釈天|qq=|12=draft}}.

=== Choosing a Day ===
Gengshen days occur on the sixth day (excluding intercalary days {{ill|Intercalary Day|ja|間日|qq=|12=draft}}) of the {{ill|Hassen|ja|八専|qq=|12=draft}} cycle.
