{{Sexagenary cycle comprehensive|qq=}} '''Yang Metal Monkey also known as Gengshen''' (庚申; かのえさる、こうきんのさる、こうしん) is one of the [[:en:Sexagenary cycle|Sexagenary cycle]].
It is the 57th combination in the Sexagenary cycle comprehensive, preceded by {{ill|Kimi|ja|1=Yin Earth Goat|2=ja|己未|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kimi|qq=}} and followed by {{ill|Shinyuu|ja|1=Yin Metal Rooster|2=ja|辛酉|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shinyuu|qq=}}. In {{ill|Yin-Yang Five Elements|ja|陰陽五行|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yin-Yang Five Elements|qq=}}, the stem {{ill|Geng|ja|庚|1=Kanoe (庚)|lt=Kanoe (庚)|2=ja|3=庚|4=zh|5=庚|1=Kanoe (庚)|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Geng|13=User:Immanuelle/Kanoe (庚)|qq=}} of the [[:en:Heavenly Stems|Ten Heavenly Stems]] represents Yang Metal, and the branch [[:en:Monkey (zodiac)|Monkey (申)]] of the [[:en:Earthly Branches|Twelve Earthly Branches]] also represents Yang Metal, a state referred to as {{ill|Bihwa|ja|五行思想#比和（ひわ）|1=比和|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)#Harmonious Relationship (比和)|2=ja|3=五行思想#比和（ひわ）|lt=Harmonious Relationship (Five Elements)|qq=Bihwa|lt_ja=比和|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Bihwa|13=User:Immanuelle/比和|qq=}}.
== Gengshen Years == [[:en:Common Era|Common Era]] and [[:en:Japanese imperial year|Imperial Era]] designate years that are multiples of 60 as [[:en:Year|Year]] of Gengshen.
=== Nature and Era Change === Because both the heavenly stem and earthly branch of Gengshen are of [[:en:Metal|Metal]] nature, it was believed that the metal energy pervading the universe in a Gengshen year or day would render human hearts cold and unfeeling. The following combination, {{ill|Shinyuu|ja|1=Yin Metal Rooster|2=ja|辛酉|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shinyuu|qq=}}, also being metal in nature—with Xin being of Yin energy—was thought to intensify this coldness. Consequently, Gengshen and Shinyuu were considered harbingers of political upheaval, and to avert such changes it was not uncommon to change eras for two consecutive years. For example, this occurred in the first years of [[:en:Man'en|Man'en]] ([[:en:1860|1860]]) and [[:en:Bunkyū|Bunkyu]] ([[:en:1861|1861]]).
