== Gengshen Month == In years where the last digit of the Western Calendar year is 3 or 8 (when the heavenly stem is {{ill|Guǐ|ja|癸|1=Mizunoto (癸)|lt=Mizunoto (癸)|2=ja|3=癸|4=zh|5=癸|1=Mizunoto (癸)|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Guǐ|13=User:Immanuelle/Mizunoto (癸)|qq=}} or {{ill|Wu|ja|戊|1=Tsuchinoe (戊)|lt=Tsuchinoe (戊)|2=ja|3=戊|4=zh|5=戊|1=Tsuchinoe (戊)|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Wu|13=User:Immanuelle/Tsuchinoe (戊)|qq=}}), the month of [[:en:July|July]] becomes the Gengshen [[:en:Month|Month (Calendar)]]. Note that here the month may refer either to a month of the {{ill|Japanese Lunisolar Calendar|ja|旧暦|1=Japanese Lunisolar Calendar|1=Japanese Lunisolar Calendar|11=Japanese Lunisolar Calendar|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Japanese Lunisolar Calendar|13=User:Immanuelle/Japanese Lunisolar Calendar|qq=}} or to a {{ill|Seasonal Month|ja|節月|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Seasonal Month|qq=}} (from [[:en:Liqiu|Start of Autumn]] until the day before [[:en:Bailu (solar term)|White Dew]]).
== Gengshen Day == On Gengshen days, a Gengshen Vigil ({{ill|Gengshen Vigil|ja|庚申待|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Gengshen Vigil|qq=}}, also known as {{ill|Gengshen Lecture|ja|庚申講|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Gengshen Lecture|qq=}}) was held. {{main|[[:en:Kōshin|Gengshen Faith]]|qq=}}
A Gengshen day is also the [[:en:Ennichi|Festival Day]] of [[:en:Śakra (Buddhism)|Taishakuten]].
=== Choosing a Day === Gengshen days occur on the sixth day (excluding intercalary days {{ill|Intercalary Day|ja|間日|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Intercalary Day|qq=}}) of the {{ill|Hassen|ja|八専|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hassen|qq=}} cycle. == See Also == * {{prefix|qq=}} * {{intitle|qq=}}
